Modified    : two local modifications; reapply both when upgrading.
              1. One mechanical rename so protoc's C# generator accepts the files: the empty message `void`
                 (api_options.proto) is renamed `Void`, and the 50 `returns (void)` in api.proto become `returns (Void)`.
                 `void` is a C# keyword and generates uncompilable code. The wire format is unchanged (empty message).
              2. `option csharp_namespace = "WindowsBtProxy.Api.Proto";` added to both files (after the syntax/import lines),
                 so the generated types (LogLevel, Void, ...) do not live in the global namespace and shadow
                 Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.LogLevel / System.Void. No wire impact.
              To upgrade, re-fetch both files from a newer tag, reapply both modifications, and update this file.
